  "notes": "b=1: one KV-cached decode step at position 255 (prefix cached per athlete, own precision). b=256: one 256-token prefill forward with full logits. Inputs are held-out val tokens. mlx_gpu_bf16 is extra: the pilot's own training/inference dtype. q8/q4 = nn.quantize (group 64, affine) on every Linear incl. lm_head and on the token embedding, fp32 activations. Core ML packages are fp16. Core ML decode is stateless with the KV cache as I/O: a 255-token prefix package returns K/V (own fp16 precision, kept host-side as fp32 numpy), and every timed step passes the full past K/V (2 x 6x3x255x128 fp32 = 4.7 MB) in and gets logits + new K/V out; MLX/numpy keep their cache on-device/in-process. bpb at 256-token context is higher than the README's 1.167 (1024 context, bf16). numpy and mlx_cpu differ from mlx_gpu by 0.033 in logits at b=256 (and 0.008 at b=1 through the 255-token prefix): MLX GPU fp32 matmul with >= 8 rows is TF32-class (see e26 notes), so the reference, not the CPU engines, carries that error.",
